# ── _start_session_watchdog: the single watchdog-ownership decision (s18 rework) ──
# The plan's no-double-run non-negotiable made STRUCTURAL: EXACTLY ONE watchdog per
# session — the aewatch daemon under AE_WATCHDOG_IMPL=uv (bash stands down), else the
# bash per-session watchdog; a disabled watchdog (meta/config false) starts NEITHER.
# Driven behaviorally: a fake ${AE_META}/watchdog executable records a bash start, a
# stubbed hook records an aewatch start; exactly one (or none) may fire.
eval "$(awk '/^_start_session_watchdog\(\) \{/,/^\}$/' <<<"$AE_SOURCE")"
